;;; -*- mode: lisp; base: 10; syntax: common-lisp; -*-
;;; system/core/runtime/supplement.dict
;;;
;;; SUPPLEMENTARY lexicon -- common words that are NOT in Marcus's verbatim
;;; dictionary (defs-dictionary.dict) but come up when parsing everyday
;;; example sentences. This file is OURS, not Marcus's: his
;;; defs-dictionary.dict stays pristine, and vocabulary he simply never
;;; entered is added here instead. Each form only ADDS a word; nothing
;;; here overrides a Marcus definition.
;;;
;;; Loaded by `load-supplement' (dictionary.lisp) immediately AFTER the
;;; canonical dictionary, so the `jlike' targets below (block, boy, ...)
;;; already exist. It is read with the same MacLISP-flavored readtable as
;;; defs-dictionary.dict and the same definers from lexicon.lisp; the
;;; loader binds *package* to :parsifal, so (like the canonical file) this
;;; is data only -- no in-package form.
;;;
;;;   `jlike NEW OLD'  makes NEW share OLD's features, markers and case
;;;                    frame -- the cheapest faithful way to add a word.
;;;   Useful targets in Marcus's dict:
;;;     block  -- (noun ns n3p) markers (inanim physob)   [count thing]
;;;     boy    -- (noun ns n3p) markers (hanim physob)     [human]
;;;
;;; When you hit a missing word, prefer adding one line here over editing
;;; Marcus's source.

;; --- common nouns Marcus didn't enter ---
(jlike hair block)      ; inanimate physobj count noun  (cf. "...with the red hair")
(jlike tree block)      ; inanimate physobj count noun
(jlike friend boy)      ; human animate noun
